t","items":[{"text":"Strong English"},{"text":"Regional language"},{"text":"At least one foreign language for international tourism"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Target progression"},{"type":"flow","items":["Tourism + history + destination fundamentals","2027–28: Guiding + storytelling + hospitality + first aid","2028–29: Specialised destination training + internship","2029–30: Tour Guide / Tourism Executive","2030–33: Professional Tour Guide / Destination Specialist","2033–36: Senior Guide / Tour Manager","2036–40: Destination Manager / Tourism Programme Manager","2040–46: Tourism Business Leader / Destination Consultant / Travel Entrepreneur"],"label":"2026–27:"},{"type":"h","text":"Best employability combination"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA Tourism & Hospitality","Destination Specialisation","Tour Guiding Skills","First Aid","Foreign Language","Storytelling","Digital Tourism","Practical Field Experience"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"note","label":"Key principle","text":"A great Tour Guide does more than provide information. The professional must turn destination knowledge into an engaging, accurate, safe and personalised experience while respecting local communities, culture, heritage and the environment."}]}]}